  <section class="section alt" id="where-it-runs" aria-labelledby="h-runs">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="kicker">Where it runs</p>
      <h2 id="h-runs">One HTTP endpoint, and nothing else listens</h2>
      <p class="intro">App code never leaves the system; the browser receives the view and the data the app chose to bind. No middleware, no extra server, no BTP subscription, no frontend deployment.</p>
      <div class="flow">
        <div class="box">
          <h3>Browser</h3>
          <ol><li>Generic UI5 shell<small>loaded once, the same for every app; no app code of its own</small></li></ol>
        </div>
        <div class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</div>
        <div class="box server">
          <h3>SAP system — the only server</h3>
          <ol>
            <li>ICF node → abap2UI5 handler → your app class</li>
            <li>SAP logon, authorization objects, sy-uname</li>
            <li>App state in one table, per user</li>
          </ol>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="split">
        <dl class="facts-list">
          <dt>Systems</dt>
          <dd><ul class="chips"><li>S/4HANA Public Cloud</li><li>BTP ABAP Environment</li><li>S/4HANA Private Cloud &amp; on-premise</li><li>NetWeaver 7.02 or later</li></ul></dd>
          <dt>UI5</dt>
          <dd>The frontend is UI5 itself, 1.71 to 2.x. By default it loads from the public CDN; a productive installation points it at the UI5 the system already ships, which is what a system without internet access uses.</dd>
          <dt>Where an app appears</dt>
          <dd><ul class="chips"><li>Browser tab</li><li>Fiori launchpad tile</li><li>SAP Build Work Zone</li><li>Microsoft Teams</li><li>Microsoft Excel</li><li>iOS &amp; Android</li><li>Inside your own UI5 app</li></ul></dd>
        </dl>
        <div class="card">
          <h3 class="first">What Basis does — all of it</h3>
          <ol class="steps-basis">
            <li>Pull the package with abapGit</li>
            <li>Create the ICF node and put an authorization object on it</li>
            <li>Change the four production defaults in the user exit: UI5 source, error details, the Content Security Policy, the node authorization</li>
            <li>Optionally switch on the monitor</li>
          </ol>
          <p class="after">No job to schedule and no schema to migrate on upgrade.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="more">→ More on <a href={`${DOCS}configuration/productive_usage`}>Productive Usage</a>, <a href={`${DOCS}configuration/ui5_versions`}>UI5 Versions</a>, <a href={`${DOCS}configuration/performance`}>Performance</a> and <a href={`${DOCS}integration/`}>Integration</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" id="what-it-costs" aria-labelledby="h-cost">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="kicker">What it costs</p>
      <h2 id="h-cost">No license fee, now or later — while commercial platforms charge every year</h2>
      <div class="split">
        <div class="price">
          <span class="big">0 <small>license fees</small></span>
          <ul>
            <li>MIT licensed, commercial use included</li>
            <li>No license key, no subscription</li>
            <li>No per-user, per-system or per-app fee</li>
            <li>Runs on the ABAP stack and the UI5 version you already have</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="prose">
          <p>The apps built with it are standard UI5 freestyle apps, licensed the way your organization licenses every other UI5 app.</p>
          <p>Commercial SAP app platforms charge per named user or per device, every month, often with minimum terms and setup fees - and the bill grows with every user who adopts the apps. With abap2UI5 adoption costs nothing.</p>
          <p><b>What is not free is the work:</b> an ABAP developer's time to write the screen, and the evenings of the volunteers who maintain the framework. Support is the community's, on GitHub issues and Slack, on a best-effort basis; there is no vendor SLA to buy from the project. Companies and freelancers offer paid implementation, training and support agreements around it.</p>
          <p class="more">→ More on the <a href={`${DOCS}resources/license`}>License</a> and <a href={`${DOCS}resources/support`}>Support</a>.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <h3 class="calc-title">Work it out for your landscape</h3>
      <p class="intro">Set the sliders to your landscape, tick your systems and your support, pick a currency, press Calculate.</p>
      <CostCalculator />
    </div>
  </section>

